{
  "summary": "Static source inspection maps a possible path from the MCP caller through index readiness, query processing, retrieval and answer generation. It does not establish that the sample is read-only when invoked: repository loading or indexing may change files, and a query with a session ID attempts to persist a dialogue turn. No target code was executed and no tests were run.",
  "conclusions": [
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "The supplied MCP caller, code_qa, obtains a FastCode instance, calls _ensure_repos_ready and _ensure_loaded, creates or reuses a session ID, then calls FastCode.query with question, ready repository names as repo_filter, the session ID and multi_turn. It formats the returned answer and sources as a string. The implementations of the two readiness helpers are not supplied.",
      "source_ids": ["3bdeac89956f17801807b9abaeba7a998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c3e2c916f566"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "FastCode.query checks self.repo_indexed before its try block and raises RuntimeError if false. That flag is the shown query gate, not evidence that every requested index is valid or loaded.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "When agency mode is enabled on the retriever and an iterative agent exists, FastCode.query creates a minimal ProcessedQuery and skips QueryProcessor.process. Otherwise it calls QueryProcessor.process with the question, dialogue summaries and LLM enhancement enabled. The conditions are checked in query; the actual processing implementation is not supplied.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "The shown query path passes the ProcessedQuery, ordinary filters, repo_filter, agency-mode override and optional dialogue summaries to retriever.retrieve. It passes the original question, retrieval output, ProcessedQuery.to_dict(), full dialogue history and optional prompt_builder to AnswerGenerator.generate. Query-result cache lookup and writeback appear only in commented-out code in this method.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "Shown retrieval helpers apply distinct boundaries: _apply_filters requires exact language and type matches and a file_path substring match; _semantic_search passes repo_filter into vector-store search and checks returned repo names again; _final_repo_filter removes results whose element repo_name is not selected. Their definitions do not establish which helpers retriever.retrieve calls, or in what order.",
      "source_ids": ["42e32ad5d9ffdb60e15ef62b7fcc5804da659c2f14129552fead458bfdec396e", "c4c8a1aae4e8162a15519af3e047c6c6950e9881997bcb98432ee4e2f3aeaa66", "ff351f4dfda0da31e1e6f6f083b5adb3680d261d105c6e41f7abf63a8caa8648"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "The supplied agency helper reconstructs a ProcessedQuery, calls iterative_agent.retrieve_with_iteration when available and returns its results. If the agent is absent or that call raises, it returns its original results instead. The supplied first-round agent method builds a prompt, calls an LLM and parses its response; these definitions show possible branches, not that they ran for this sample.",
      "source_ids": ["e7510cca5235adc213f163d7d6130ce424c3c74615346a2a807d73fcddc3627c", "7a8f6ee0a73ec62b07c2dfddb4314b98777920798c7a71aad0ac4817b32d9257"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "AnswerGenerator.generate prepares context from retrieved elements, builds either a caller-supplied prompt or its default prompt, counts tokens, selects a configured provider and returns an answer dictionary with retrieval count, token count and extracted sources on its ordinary return path. The context-preparation and prompt-building implementations are not supplied, so the precise material sent to a model cannot be verified.",
      "source_ids": ["958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "FastCode.query owns the local processed_query, retrieved list and result for a call. Its retriever, generator and cache manager are instance attributes; when enable_multi_turn is omitted, the method reads a configuration default. With multi-turn enabled and a session ID, it fetches recent summaries for retrieval and separately obtains full dialogue history for generation.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "The MCP caller generates an eight-character UUID-derived session ID if none is passed and passes an ID to query even when multi_turn is false. FastCode.query attempts to save a dialogue turn whenever session_id is present, including single-turn calls; it stores the answer, summary, formatted sources and metadata rather than the raw retrieved list.",
      "source_ids": ["3bdeac89956f17801807b9abaeba7a998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c3e2c916f566", "3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "CacheManager.save_dialogue_turn returns false when disabled and otherwise builds turn data, calls self.set, updates a session index and returns true unless an exception occurs. It does not check the return value of self.set; FastCode.query likewise does not check save_dialogue_turn's return value before logging that the turn was saved. A returned answer or that log message therefore does not establish durable session persistence.",
      "source_ids": ["18bd1442ebf14ca13388be94fcc2884400bbcbd9d893e24058b3934245f40f20", "3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "A local repository load is not inherently read-only: RepositoryLoader.load_from_path copies the entire working tree, including untracked files, into a workspace with symlinks preserved, unless source and destination are the same path. Its destination-preparation method backs up an existing destination. The API's load-and-index route also invokes indexing and invalidates a vector-store scan cache.",
      "source_ids": ["3ea8337a4cc79f1c2bcb7141801a9fd23b61a3ed19eae6baa193e997c63c4aad", "f30079af74f72d237599ee302df22093afc8fcfcef16cff1f5f54a8adeaf237a", "a97fd76745148e7c4cf04cd0fc6ef8a3f759b783ada1e4e66578165b20428ad0"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "The supplied persistence methods write vector indexes and metadata, BM25 data or graph data to disk, subject to their respective guards and error handling. The MCP reindex_repo caller explicitly loads a repository, forces indexing, then clears in-memory loaded/indexed state. These are separate mutation paths to account for before adapting a read-only sample.",
      "source_ids": ["0d0864e396269bcb455b2662e28f479a30dc0df72b55b79a038c4703d11862ec", "2a6b1d5e31cbaca965ffb0ed0009e8ba4bcb9d9091b0a2d7ce5912644e474bd9", "a8f62f0083e424b3040b89ae0b66c4ea0c393149f664bb4bfe141baa5fa4be7e", "539e660bfb0243dfa94d4a024e7f03bf6acbdc2c921ddad4825fe586ba7f10e6"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "FastCode.query converts exceptions raised inside its try block into a dictionary containing answer and error. Its repo_indexed check and optional recent-summary fetch occur before that try block, so exceptions there are not converted by this method. The MCP caller formats result.get('answer') and appends a session ID without inspecting result['error']; returned text alone does not prove a successful query.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c", "3bdeac89956f17801807b9abaeba7a998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c3e2c916f566"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "AnswerGenerator.generate catches exceptions only around provider invocation, response handling and result construction; context preparation, prompt construction, token counting and truncation precede its try block. On a caught failure it returns an error-bearing answer dictionary. An unconfigured provider instead produces an error string as raw_response on the ordinary path; missing OpenAI or Anthropic clients also return error strings rather than raising.",
      "source_ids": ["958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d", "64e53597abdf83d3827430a880cb98d05ad1364d9d46aca28b995d8e140a279e", "7dbc6309168db0b0fdf528caeb2dd6ee65b604ae89d35cd3160bb3c9816f8c96"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "Generation calculates available input tokens as max_context_tokens minus max_tokens and reserve_tokens. If the initial prompt exceeds that amount, it budgets context after estimating a no-context prompt, truncates context from the end or removes it, then recounts the rebuilt prompt. The shown code does not reject an over-limit final prompt; a large question, history or custom prompt can remain a boundary even after context removal.",
      "source_ids": ["958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d", "6e88811451cda06d0d7c8b87b79fde3880f897677a4c59d2e8b445cb70fabc30"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "OpenAI and Anthropic non-streaming helpers raise for empty or incomplete provider responses and re-raise caught provider exceptions, allowing generate's inner catch to handle them. Their separate streaming helpers yield textual error messages on failures; the supplied generate method calls the non-streaming helpers, not those streaming methods.",
      "source_ids": ["64e53597abdf83d3827430a880cb98d05ad1364d9d46aca28b995d8e140a279e", "7dbc6309168db0b0fdf528caeb2dd6ee65b604ae89d35cd3160bb3c9816f8c96", "e3e2f3413e163267a24a860ef94e98e87a611a4880628e0555a534f94402de10", "4c2bdef3d031d1e22c45de1bec93f183c88aa6aa935f8cf5357a8fc871f31fd0", "958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "scope_and_verification",
      "text": "CodeParser.parse_file dispatches by extension-derived language to Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, C/C++, Rust or C# parsers, and uses a generic parser otherwise. CodeIndexer.index_files skips a file when reading or parsing returns None, then embeds elements it did index. This is parser-routing evidence, not proof that all repository files or Python constructs were successfully represented.",
      "source_ids": ["895930b6378e96bcc4e2cb5369b44aa1d53e9e2f363a2a55a2e8a0c877dee63b", "2dff45803c5c2609981a1dac4cbdcbf1f712a465199acef081018a2e3712cfde"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "scope_and_verification",
      "text": "The supplied parser also defines a narrow textual repair for duplicate 'as' clauses in exception handlers, while CallExtractor._execute_query catches Tree-sitter query errors and returns an empty capture list. No supplied call site establishes whether the repair ran on this sample. A parsed or retrieved snippet must not be treated as proof that the original code is valid or executable.",
      "source_ids": ["16f555bbef39f866b83fd033ea08bacc47b239785b29f138c159da80d03911a0", "0c7aa1f17802658fd8f479572794f6eb00095f3eb6e7a55d17ced456b50ed1b5"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "scope_and_verification",
      "text": "AgentTools.search_codebase checks its root with _is_safe_path, resolves it, walks matching files, reads text with decoding errors ignored and returns bounded line snippets; unreadable content can still produce a filename match. Because the path-safety and resolution helpers are not supplied, this method alone cannot establish the filesystem boundary for symlinks or every requested root.",
      "source_ids": ["9ff64131bff3dc5629571f485b5ed9de696ddc09605310793c3ccdf0002e7a8b"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "scope_and_verification",
      "text": "For follow-up source inspection, the supplied callers and callees point first to _ensure_repos_ready, _ensure_loaded, FastCode initialization/loading/indexing, QueryProcessor.process, HybridRetriever.retrieve, vector-store search, generator context/prompt helpers, and session-index/cache methods. The supplied methods establish why these boundaries matter, but do not supply their implementations or any test entry point.",
      "source_ids": ["3bdeac89956f17801807b9abaeba7a998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c3e2c916f566", "3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c", "958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d", "18bd1442ebf14ca13388be94fcc2884400bbcbd9d893e24058b3934245f40f20"]
    }
  ],
  "unknowns": [
    "The supplied source set does not include _ensure_repos_ready or _ensure_loaded. It cannot verify how code_qa decides readiness, which files it may create, or whether an existing index is valid. The separate _is_repo_indexed helper checks only for two persisted file paths.",
    "HybridRetriever.retrieve, QueryProcessor.process, vector-store search, AnswerGenerator._prepare_context, _build_prompt and token helpers are absent. Their call order, result conversions, actual filter application and effective context cannot be verified.",
    "FastCode initialization, load_repository, index_repository, _get_full_dialogue_history, _get_next_turn_number, cache self.set and session-index updates are absent. Successful indexing, durable persistence and session-history behavior remain unverified.",
    "The supplied coverage reports 81 parsed files, 40 skipped files and no failed files; it does not explain skipped-file contents or prove source-wide completeness. No target code was executed, and no compilation, provider request or tests were performed."
  ]
}
